# Lord Vatticus
dre.vatticus.step.carcinus=Lord Vatticus: start with the sea. Hunt crabs, gather claws for a lair map and find the burrow of Carcinus on the shore. Only crab weapons pierce his shell.
dre.vatticus.step.snow_glacon=Lord Vatticus: the Deep Shell opens the snow dungeon beneath a winter forest. The Snow Glacon dwells there, and only he holds the Snow Globe, the key to Iceika. Bring fire: he fears it.
dre.vatticus.step.lich_king=Lord Vatticus: in Iceika the Lich King sits on the shoulder of the Frost Colossus at the Frozen Throne. A throne map is made from ice shards. Dress warmly: the cold kills faster than blades.
dre.vatticus.step.ancient_entity=Lord Vatticus: the throne shards remember the Ancient Entity. Build the Mysterious Clock from them and wake it in the Overworld. After it, the End opens.
dre.vatticus.step.watcher=Lord Vatticus: in the End, ender watchers carry an eye. With snowflakes it makes the Call of the Watcher. The Call sounds only in the Watcher's Observatory deep in the Nether - a map of paper in nether bricks shows it. Its Eye opens your way here, to Arcana.
dre.vatticus.step.cadillion_eden=Lord Vatticus: you are in Arcana, but the world is wider. The Wanderer's Clock opens Eden. The Great Cadillion lives in a sacred grove high above the islands - its giant trees are visible from afar. Make a Call from the world's souls and gem and offer it on the altar by the ancient shrine in the glade. A grove map - paper in Eden fragments - shows the way. In battle it lowers its horn and charges - dodge so it crashes into a trunk or a column: stunned, it is defenceless. The Call needs a sanctum seal - it lies in the dungeons inside the islands - and a horn of the world's cadillions. Temper the world's armor with its mobs' materials - it protects from the cadillion's main trick. Eden ore yields only to an Eden pickaxe: make the first one from its mobs' souls (soul - fragment); stone needs a Divine pickaxe.
dre.vatticus.step.cadillion_wildwood=Lord Vatticus: the Eden time gear raises the clock to Wildwood, and the Eden guardian heart surrounded by Eden gem blocks gives gate stones for the portal frame. Wildwood armor, weapons and tools are made from the same Eden items, chunks and mob materials, handles from Wildwood sticks. The Wildwood grove is guarded by the Ancient Golem: its body cannot be pierced while its arms and legs stand - strike them. What you break first decides how it fights at the end.
dre.vatticus.step.cadillion_apalachia=Lord Vatticus: next is Apalachia. The Wildwood gear and guardian heart, the clock, gate stones, the grove, the Call on the altar - you know the way. The Apalachia grove is held by the Warrior King. He does not fall the first time: he rises thrice, angrier each time. His wave throws you off the island - keep to the center or wear the Apalachia set.
dre.vatticus.step.cadillion_skythern=Lord Vatticus: Skythern, the sky world. Its grove is guarded by the Wind Lord - no weapon touches him. Four wind totems will rise around at different heights: reach one, touch it and hold your ground while it charges - it strikes the Lord with lightning. The carpet in the Skythern set lifts you to any totem.
dre.vatticus.step.twilight_demon=Lord Vatticus: Mortum, the world of darkness. The Twilight Demon rules there. His crystal answers only in the Demonic Circle above the islands - a map to the circle made of Mortum fragments shows the way. Twice he will offer to part: leave him be - he goes, giving part of the spoils; strike - the fight goes on, the dark thickens, but he gives everything. Without his defeat armor will not take Mortum tempering.
dre.vatticus.step.karot=Lord Vatticus: Karot remains. His crystal also wakes only in the Demonic Circle. Karot is a mirror: he strikes like your weapon and holds like your armor. Come weak - the fight is easy, but the spoils are modest. Defeat him - and Halite becomes part of your armor.
dre.vatticus.step.end=Lord Vatticus: you have come further than any Wanderer before you. Beyond lies the dream world, Vethea. Its secrets I will not reveal yet.
dre.vatticus.tip.scorchers=Tip: in the Nether, in the Fire Chamber, the King of Scorchers waits - the Infernal Flame kindles only there (map: paper in blaze powder). Defeating him unlocks the fire protection perk.
dre.vatticus.tip.statues=Tip: do not shelve boss statues - the War General grants a heart for each.
dre.vatticus.tip.leorna=Tip: Leorna pays for the fish of the day, and gives a golden rod for the tenth.
dre.vatticus.tip.merik=Tip: Captain Merik reforges Divine swords, and each world's weapons have their own modifier.
dre.vatticus.tip.orders=Tip: the War General hands out hunting orders, rewarding service with ranks and weapons.
